## Provenance

AWS publishes the Session Manager control plane (StartSession, ResumeSession,
TerminateSession, plus StreamUrl/TokenValue) but not a specification for the
data-channel wire protocol. The protocol implemented here was learned from the
following open-source sources, and this project is a derivative of what they
document and implement:

- aws/session-manager-plugin (Apache License 2.0) - the reference client;
  header layout, handshake, acknowledgements/retransmission, KMS handshake.
- aws/amazon-ssm-agent (Apache License 2.0) - the protocol peer.
- hupe1980/aws-ssm-bridge (MIT) - the published "Wire protocol" notes that
  document the format by observation, including the MessageId byte order and
  the base64 `[]byte` handshake encoding.
- dacort/pyssm-client (Apache License 2.0) - an independent Python client,
  including base64-in-band file transfer.

This project makes no clean-room claim. Per-file provenance notes are added
when logic is transliterated rather than re-derived; if any Apache-2.0 source
is transliterated, the Apache License 2.0 text is included alongside this
NOTICE, as that license requires.
